ote card on a wooden bench](assets/images/voice-note-capture.webp)\n\nTall grasses create a quiet corner without a wall. Ask Maya whether the visual\nlanguage can represent *degrees of invitation* rather than activity categories.\n\nCaptured during [the field day](/note/journal/2026-08-27_field_day). Process into\n[the data dictionary](/note/projects/neighborhood_atlas/data_dictionary) after consent review.","tags":["inbox","observation","fieldwork"],"aliases":[],"status":"","avatarUrl":"","createdAt":"2026-08-28T22:00:42.000Z","modifiedAt":"2026-09-05T10:20:29.812Z","contentPath":"/generated/notes/1cbbbcc9257a01119b4e66d4dd124d94a42563b28f88d062a397ff9034c874ab.json","wordCount":50,"readingMinutes":1,"pinned":false},{"id":"stash/wayfinding_reference","section":"stash","sectionLabel":"Stash","relativePath":"wayfinding_reference.md","sourceFile":"stash/wayfinding_reference.md","route":"/note/stash/wayfinding_reference","title":"Wayfinding reference","excerpt":"https://www.nngroup.com/articles/wayfinding/","preview":"https://www.nngroup.com/articles/wayfinding/\n\nA quick reminder that a map is also an invitation: people need to know where\nto begin, what choices they have, and how to leave without feeling lost.\n\nPull one useful idea into [Design principles](/note/notes/design_principles) before\nthe next prototype pass. No need to preserve the whole article if the note only\nturns into a single sentence.","tags":["inbox","web","design","atlas"],"aliases":[],"status":"","avatarUrl":"","createdAt":"2026-08-28T22:00:42.000Z","modifiedAt":"2026-08-31T10:22:58.470Z","contentPath":"/generated/notes/52093ab287f8c5453871890e712f34200e99d3bb36a687e3cf0f0588d3c1975a.json","wordCount":57,"readingMinutes":1,"pinned":false},{"id":"playlists/fieldwork_inspiration/power_of_vulnerability","section":"playlists","sectionLabel":"Playlists","relativePath":"fieldwork_inspiration/power_of_vulnerability.md","sourceFile":"playlists/fieldwork_inspiration/power_of_vulnerability.md","route":